      "textEn": "124\n\nMan, in reality, becomes intelligent and dedicated to God. This is the only way to stop the cycle of birth and death. Its confirmation is from the teachings given by Shri Chaitanya Mahaprabhu to Srila Rup Goswami at Dashashwamedh Ghat.\n(Chaitanya Charitamrita, Middle 19.11)—\n\nWho is fortunate to be deluded by the universe? Devotion-leaf-seed-of-foot-of-Guru-Krishna-by-Praise. The soul keeps wandering in various forms and bodies in many worlds, and if by chance\nit comes into contact with a genuine guru, then by the grace of the guru, it attains refuge in Shri Krishna\nand its devotional life begins. When one does not see the consequences of their actions,\nbeing selfish, negligent, and hasty in judgment.\nPast memories are destroyed there by heat.\nHaving consumed, he knows the abode of sexual intercourse. 7>. Meaning of the word\n\nYada—When; Na—Not; Pashyati—Sees; Ayatha—Unnecessarily; Guna-ehaam—Attempt of sensory gratification; Swa-Artha—Self-interest;\nMa—In; Pramaat—Crazy; Sahasa—Quickly; Vipashchit—Even the wise; Gata-Smritiha—Having lost memory; Vindati—Finds; Tatra—There;\nTapana—Suffering; Asadya—Having attained; Maithunyaam—Dependent on sexual intercourse; Agaram—House; Ajnaha—Out of ignorance..\n\nEven if someone is very learned and clever, if he does not understand that\nthe efforts made for sensual pleasure are a waste of time, then he is mad. He\nForgetting self-interest, in this world, being dominated by sensual desires and the abode of all material sufferings,\nHe wants to remain happy by being attached to his home. In this way, man is like a foolish animal.\nIs. Note: A person in a lower state of devotion (adhama) is not considered a pure devotee.\nWithout desire for others,\nbeing free from knowledge, action, and other obstacles—to be a pure devotee, a person should be free from all material desires,\nand he should not even touch action and dry knowledge. In a lower state, sometimes there may be interest in philosophical