      "textEn": "132\n\nNot stay. Those who are engrossed in sin and virtuous deeds, should engage in devotion in every way. They should always avoid desire-driven actions. If a disciple, son, or subject, who is devoid of divine vision,\nis put into the bondage of karma, how will he benefit? This is like taking a blind man\nto a dark well and letting him fall. Meaning: The Bhagavad Gita (3.26) says—\n\nNa buddhibhedam janayedajnanam karmasanginam. One who performs all actions with enthusiasm, having made a wise decision, should practice. “A wise man should not create confusion in the minds of ignorant people who are attached to desire-driven actions.\nThat is, he should not turn them away from action. Rather, he should engage them in action with devotion through his conduct.”\n\nPeople themselves are the best, destroyer of sight-\nRyoharthansmehet nikamakamah.\nOne who is without enmity, who does not know the cause of happiness and sorrow,\nis ignorant. 16. Meaning of the word\n\nLokah - people; Swayam - oneself; Shreyasi - of the path of welfare; Nashtadrishtih - those whose vision has been destroyed; Yah - who; Arthaan -\nobjects of worldly enjoyment; Samihet - desire; Nikama - lustful; Nikama - lustful;\nAnyon-vairah - jealous of each other; Sukha-lesha-hetoh - only for momentary pleasure; Ananta-dukham - immense suffering; Cha - also;\nNa - not; Veda - know; Mudhah - foolish people, ignorant. Due to ignorance, a materialistic person does not understand his true benefit, which is the path of life.\nIt is a beneficial path. He remains bound by the desires of material pleasures, and all his\nplans are prepared for this one task. Such a person, for momentary pleasure, is antagonistic.\nHe creates society, and due to his mentality, he jumps into the ocean of sorrow. Such a fool does not even know this.\nMeaning: Nashtadrishti: The meaning of the word is, \"one who cannot see the future,\" and this word is very meaningful in this verse. Pranas keep moving from one body to another, and the good or bad fruits of the deeds done in this life\nare received in this birth, otherwise in the next birth. Who is ignorant and"
